[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3]

; The floor's NAVMESH lives beside its markers, because the walkable cave IS
; level authoring — one asset says where the chest, the dens, and the ground
; are. Every peer loads this scene locally (cave_load_scenery); only the HOST
; queries it, from the authority-only brain tick, so pathing never hits the
; wire. Shape: one floor minus a RIFT at x 380..430, y 60..300, tiled by eight
; rectangles that share WHOLE edges so the region merges without leaning on
; edge_connection_margin. North and south ledges keep both chambers mutually
; reachable — the rift is a detour, never a barrier, because a wave stranded
; on the wrong side would deadlock the floor-cleared gate in cave_host_tick.
